# CABLE KNEE STRIKE

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Cable Knee Strike is an explosive resistance exercise designed to develop hip flexion power, trunk stiffness and force transmission during knee strikes.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the highest-transfer resistance exercises for improving close-range striking power and clinch performance.

---

# Philosophy

A powerful knee strike is generated by the entire body.

The supporting leg creates force against the ground, the hips accelerate forward, the trunk stabilizes the movement and the knee is driven explosively toward the target.

The Cable Knee Strike overloads this kinetic sequence while preserving sport-specific movement mechanics.

CAS uses the Cable Knee Strike to develop explosive knee strikes without compromising technical quality.

